Benefit to the insured and insurer: for the stated scenario, a tested authority check can prevent an unauthorised commitment; linked records can make investigation and recovery analysis more reliable. Fewer such events would support a frequency-reduction hypothesis. Narrower authority may restrict transaction exposure, while verified shared budgets may help manage accumulation. These are distinct propositions requiring separate evidence.

The EUR 12,000 order value is not a demonstrated EUR 12,000 avoided claim. Cancellation rights, recoveries, fulfilment, consequential damage and policy terms affect the actual loss. No expected-loss percentage or premium saving is inferred from this example.

Fair comparison: if the existing procurement platform already enforces the same limits, delegation, revocation and evidence requirements reliably across the same routes, it may block the order without GAuth. The incremental benefit must then be assessed in terms of independently evidenced business authority, consistency across systems, delegation controls and claims records—not credited again as a newly prevented loss.

For comparison, an EUR 800 purchase of the wrong component may proceed in both arrangements. It is an authorised performance error rather than an authority breach. That distinction helps the claims team investigate the relevant cause and policy section; it does not determine coverage.

5. Loss prevention: keeping delegated authority within approved limits
======================================================================

Generated plans, summaries, memory entries and sub-agent messages may contain instructions that influence later execution. “Self-generated prompt injection” and hallucination are not synonyms: investigators should identify whether instructions crossed a trust boundary or whether the event was another form of model/application error.

The proposed control principle is that generated content cannot itself mint, enlarge or override authority. A genuine extension requires an independently authenticated and authorised grant, not the agent’s claim that it needs more permission.

A pilot should demonstrate:

- child authority cannot exceed parent action/resource scope or validity;

- prompts, retrieved content, tool output and memory cannot override those restrictions;

- a plan or task assignment is not accepted as a mandate merely because an agent produced it;

- revocation and expiry remain effective through delegation and queued work;

- downstream constraints can narrow but not enlarge the effective authority;

- required platform denials and restrictions remain independently effective.

This constrains executable consequences, not all generation of malicious or false content. An injection may exploit permitted access, influence a validly authorised decision, or use an unmediated route. An over-broad mandate can authorise substantial harm.

5.1 Per-action limits are not aggregate limits
----------------------------------------------

Repeated EUR 1,000 transactions can produce much larger total exposure. Financial budgets, rate limits and multi-agent caps require separate proof of atomic shared accounting, concurrency safety, replay prevention, retries, partial failure and transaction finality. These are pilot requirements where relied upon, not assumed features of every GAuth deployment.

